 ],
 "observations": "In this run we observed the agent read nearly the whole package before each change (ck2 2.2-2.4; ck3 3.2 'Small enough to read fully'; ck8 8.4-8.13) and mostly add new modules wired in through app.py (ck4 4.6-4.9; ck5 5.8; ck6 6.11; ck7 7.13; ck8 8.20-8.29). It verified every checkpoint with the unittest suite and, from ck2 on, added its own test file except ck5 (5.11). Most failures trace to choices the spec leaves open: simulated site data (ck1, ck3), the options schema with modified_on NOT NULL (ck5 5.8, carried into ck8), and the migrations directory and fresh-install skip (ck7 7.13). In ck6 container.py's create_project was written but never called from site create/delete (6.11, 6.13). In ck8 the new host-requirement check and first-run message (8.32) broke 25 earlier tests in the grader environment; the agent had seen docker down (8.16), switched its own tests to a fake docker (8.46-8.47), and recorded that in memory (8.58-8.59). It also changed shared interfaces in ck8: format_items gained a parameter (8.30), run_command gained timeout (8.21), and self_update imported output's private _isatty (8.26)."
}